@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Upper RAM reservation component gate
+
+Run `python3 tests/host/upper-ram-reservation/check.py OUTPUT` from the source
+tree with a native C compiler. The gate extracts maintained production bodies,
+compiles them with synthetic PFN/PTE metadata and exercises their allocation,
+free, ownership, domain exhaustion, and statistics behavior. It covers title VM
+including MEM_NOZERO, both public pool ordinals, bucket reuse and reclamation,
+normal and exhausted-aperture system allocation, explicit public stack buffers,
+dedicated title TLS alignment, and relocation capacity/destinations. It also
+compiles the OFF profile and checks the existing 64/128 policies.
+
+The fixture substitutes serialization and the existing privileged relocation
+copy/PTE/TLB backend; production search, preflight, owners and counters execute.
+Native fixed mappings stand in for CPU page walks. This is component evidence,
+not an emulator boot, x86 TLB proof, or game qualification.
+
+Run `python3 tests/host/upper-ram-reservation/check-config.py OUTPUT` with the
+production cross toolchain and CMake installed. This configures the actual tree
+to check each required allocator backend, 128-MiB capacity, the supported profile
+and the default fallback configuration.
